## Verdict

Current instruction quality: **45/100**

Main issue: the files contain reasonable generic rules, but they are **too thin to reliably steer Copilot**. They miss concrete routing to canonical docs, task-context generation, risk/approval boundaries, verification commands, ownership rules, generated-artifact policy, and adapter-specific behaviour.

VS Code supports one always-on `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, targeted `*.instructions.md` files under `.github/instructions`, and custom agents under `.github/agents`; targeted instruction files apply through `applyTo` globs or task matching, but multiple instruction files have **no guaranteed order**, so critical rules must be repeated or routed explicitly. ([Visual Studio Code][1])

